<title>USA: U.S. Aug retail sales rose 0.2 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug retail sales rose 0.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department</p>
<p>seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Aug     July--Rev from    Aug 96/95</p>
<p> Retail Sales	    0.2	0.1     0.1	   4.3</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	 0.2	0.2     0.3	   4.6</p>
<p> Auto Sales		0.1     Unch    -0.6	   3.2</p>
<p> Durable Goods	   0.3	0.1    -0.4	   5.5</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods	0.1	0.2     0.4	   3.4</p>
<p> Furniture Stores     -0.2     Unch    Unch	   2.8</p>
<p> Building Materials   -0.7	0.2    -1.6	  10.9</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Aug    July---Rev from   June--Rev from</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 205.00   204.66   204.69   204.37   204.55</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    155.33   155.07   155.50   154.76   155.08</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    49.67    49.60    49.19    49.61    49.46</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 83.78    83.55    83.09    83.47    83.40</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   121.22   121.11   121.60   120.89   121.15</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.33    11.35    11.41    11.35    11.42</p>
<p> Building Materials  11.39    11.46    11.30    11.44    11.48</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Aug     July--Rev from    Aug 96/95</p>
<p> General Merchandise   0.7	0.2     0.1	   4.8</p>
<p> Department Stores     0.9     Unch    Unch	   4.9</p>
<p> Food Stores	    -0.7	0.9     0.8	   2.6</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	 -0.7	1.1     0.9	   2.5</p>
<p> Gas Stations	   -0.9     -1.8    -0.6	   4.4</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	  1.0     -0.7    -1.6	   5.5</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places     -0.4     -0.3    Unch	  -0.9</p>
<p> Drug Stores	     0.4	1.4     1.1	   6.4</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Aug    July---Rev from    June--Rev from</p>
<p> General Merch.	25.92    25.74    25.69     25.69   25.66</p>
<p> Department Stores   20.16    19.98    19.98     19.98   19.97</p>
<p> Food Stores	   35.17    35.41    35.36     35.09   35.07</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	33.30    33.54    33.48     33.19   33.18</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  12.92    13.03    13.33     13.27   13.41</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.51     9.42     9.38	9.48    9.53</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    19.44    19.51    19.76     19.57   19.76</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    7.46     7.44     7.43	7.33    7.35</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected August retail sales to rise 0.7 percent, and, excluding autos, to be up 0.4 percent.</p>
